From 2b197252967a96888f29590cbacce726c721ef9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ientzy <ientzy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:59:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] Flash Next DFlash2: several streams, batched proposals,
 automatic width per round

Each stream gets its own drafter ring (a lane, handed out least recently used); the rings
share one storage so a round's rows draft in one batched pass. A ring counts positions from
where it started, so a stream that resumes after a cached prefix drafts from a shorter
context instead of falling back to MTP. Feature capture covers every row of a forward.

Automatic width with several rows picks one window for the round (best expected tokens
per cost over all rows); the verify forward, accept and commit then run laid out for that
window, with the GDN replay records and fold viewed at the same width. One row keeps the
full layout. NINFER_FLASH_DFLASH2_AUTO_ROWS=0 keeps several rows at full width.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
